programs.haiku:
"""Predicts layers.0.mlp.down_proj:4132 (layer 0 MLP, one rank-one piece) from the current token
and the register of the text so far.

What the component does: it is almost always near zero (std 0.04, rarely above 0.2). Its
activation is a diffuse, token-dependent signal, with a rough text-type split:
- positive on ordinary English words, most strongly on older literary words
  ("shall", "upon", "little", "young", "great", "mind", "thee", "ye", "hath");
- positive, too, in passages of older literary English, where such words are frequent so far
  in the document (the running share of them is carried from token to token);
- negative on non-Latin scripts (CJK, Cyrillic, other accented text) and on code and markup
  symbols;
- near zero, slightly positive, on spaces, digits and punctuation.

It explains well under 1% of the variance, because the component's variation is spread across
thousands of word types and context effects that no short rule captures.
"""

import re

READS = ()

OLD_WORDS = {
    "thee", "thou", "thy", "thine", "ye", "hath", "hast", "doth", "dost", "shalt", "unto",
    "whilst", "ere", "afore", "wherefore", "art", "nay", "oft", "whence", "thereof",
    "shall", "upon", "whom", "himself", "myself", "themselves", "yet", "mind", "young",
    "little", "great", "weary", "obliged", "death", "respect", "men", "may", "must",
}
CODE = re.compile(r"[{}()\[\];=<>/_#@$*&|\\`]")
ENGLISH = re.compile(r" ?[A-Za-z]+")


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    # carry: (words seen so far in this document, old-register words seen so far)
    if carry is None or prefix.position == 0 or prefix.document_ids[-1] != prefix.document_ids[-2]:
        words, old = 0, 0
    else:
        words, old = carry
    s = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    is_old = bool(ENGLISH.fullmatch(s)) and s.strip().lower() in OLD_WORDS
    if ENGLISH.fullmatch(s):
        words += 1
        old += is_old
    share = old / words if words else 0.0
    if not s.strip():
        value = 0.004
    elif any(ord(c) > 127 for c in s):
        value = -0.002
    elif CODE.search(s):
        value = -0.005
    elif s.strip().isdigit():
        value = 0.004
    elif ENGLISH.fullmatch(s):
        value = (0.05 if is_old else 0.0075) + 0.3 * share
    else:
        value = 0.003
    return (words, old), float(value)

