"""A token-local approximation: mostly zero, with negative lexical pulses.

A prominent large pulse marks an opening tool call. Truth/null literals,
weekdays, check/cross symbols, and family or romantic roles also give negative
pulses. Some
Chinese and Russian male/partner words show the same tendency. Standard C/C++
library and input-output names have fixed estimates; compound CamelCase identifiers have
a weaker length-based rule, except for positive toString conversions. These
are separate lexical sensitivities, not a claim of one shared semantic topic.
The fixed values summarize training examples; no history is needed.
"""
import re

