"""Recognize a lexical contrast, rather than infer sentence meaning.

'Between' and translations respond positively. Fixing, repairing, correcting,
and editing respond negatively; English 'fix' and Han 修 are strongest.
The spelling rules include inflections and leading code punctuation. Most
other tokens, and all contextual modulation, are approximated as zero.
Capitalization and embedding in code modestly change the strongest responses.
